\frac{(x+y)^2-2xy}{xy}
$. Since
$x+y=(xy+x+y)-x-y
=4-3xy$, $(x+y)^2=(4-3xy)^2=16-24xy+9x^2y^2$, and thus
\begin{align*}
\frac{(x+y)^2-2xy}{xy}
&=\frac{16-24xy+9x^2y^2-2xy}{xy} \\&=\frac{9x^2y^2-26xy+16}{xy}\\&=9xy-26+\frac{16}{xy}.
\end{align*>
Since $xy=\frac{3\pm\sqrt{5}}{2}$, $9xy-26+\frac{16}{xy}$ equals $9\cdot\frac{3+\sqrt{5}}{2}-26+\frac{16}{\frac{3+\sqrt{5}}{2}}$ or $9\cdot\frac{3-\sqrt{5}}{2}-2+\frac{16}{\frac{3-\sqrt{5}}{2}}$, which simplifies to $12$. <answer> $12$ </answer>

